1
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:43,500
It was filmed in 6 days for 25 thousand dollars. The government didn't want you to see it. It was banned in 23 states.
It has grossed over 600 million dollars. And it is the most profitable film in motion picture history.

2
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Inside Deep Throat is a documentary film directed by Randy Barbato.

3
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,500
In 1972, a seemingly typical shoestring budget pornographic film was made
in a Florida hotel: "Deep Throat," starring Linda Lovelace.

4
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
This film would surpass the wildest expectation of everyone involved to
become one of the most successful independent films of all time.

5
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:13,500
It caught the public imagination which met the spirit of the times, even as the self-appointed guardians of public morality struggled to
suppress it, and created, for a brief moment, a possible future where sexuality in film had a bold artistic potential.

6
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
This film covers the story of the making of this controversial film, its stunning success, its hysterical opposition
along with its dark side of mob influence and allegations of the on set mistreatment of the film's star.

7
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:28,500
Narrator (voice), played by Dennis Hopper.

